    "check": "returned unopposed: 'DONAGHADEE — No contests but there will be one new member, H. S. Cosbey' (BNL 5 May 1967 p. 5); the Belfast Telegraph, 4 May 1967, p. 11, adds that there were only eight nominations for the nine seats, all eight Independent, and that R. F. Sheldon, who did not seek re-election, would be invited to take the vacant seat (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026).",
